SECTION C — Root cause + proof the blocker is PRE-EXISTING and surface-independent
================================================================================
Crash thunk demangled (xcrun swift-demangle):
  $sSbScA_pSgIeAghyg_SbIeAghn_TR  -->
  "reabstraction thunk helper from @escaping @isolated(any) @callee_guaranteed @Sendable
   (@unowned Swift.Bool, @guaranteed Swift.Actor?) -> () to ... @Sendable (@in_guaranteed Swift.Bool) -> ()"

Trigger (BASELINE file, git-tracked, OUTSIDE this prompt's allowed files):
  apps/apple/TeslaSync/feature-views/AppearanceSettings.Controls.swift:107
      let onChange: @MainActor (Bool) -> Void
  ...:122
      Toggle("", isOn: Binding(get: { isOn }, set: onChange))
  A @MainActor (Bool)->Void used as a @Sendable Binding setter makes the compiler emit the @isolated(any)
  reabstraction thunk above; swift-frontend 6.3.2 segfaults during IRGen of that thunk. This is a toolchain
  regression (runner Swift 6.3.2 > locked Swift 6.0.1). The Checkbox surface uses a plain ((Bool)->Void)?
  — never @MainActor/@Sendable/@isolated(any) on a Bool closure — so it cannot and does not emit this thunk.

DECISIVE reproduction WITHOUT the Checkbox surface:
  1. moved all 9 Checkbox.* files OUT of the tree
  2. xcodegen generate ; xcodebuild -scheme TeslaSync -destination '...iPhone 16' build
  -> identical crash, same file:
     "Please submit a bug report ..."
     "While evaluating request IRGenRequest(IR Generation for file ".../AppearanceSettings.Controls.swift")"
     "** BUILD FAILED **"   BASELINE_EXIT=65
  (files then restored; xcodegen regenerated. The crash exists with ZERO Checkbox files present.)

